# The published site is the single self-contained index.html.
# Everything below is source-of-truth, build tooling, or sensitive
# material that should stay local and out of the public repo.

# DesignComposer source documents (landing page, prototype, pitch deck, mark)
*.dc.html
uploads/

# Un-bundled page source + DesignComposer runtime/engine
deploy-src.html
deck-stage.js
image-slot.js
/support.js

# Preview thumbnail artifact
.thumbnail

# Nested duplicate deploy trees (the served site is the repo root)
deploy/

# Nested standalone repos — separate products with their own git remotes,
# not part of the Aurelius site deploy
echoGalaxy/
Zookahs-Casino/
# PulseMask. The folder is helixPulse but the repo, the Pages path and the
# product are all "pulsemask" (github.com/ZachBach/pulsemask); the folder name
# stays put because tooling is keyed to it. Without this line `git add -A`
# from the root would embed the whole repo as a gitlink.
helixPulse/
# Brain SPECT research program (github.com/ZachBach/spect-program). Cloned here
# 2026-09-22. It will hold DICOM and NIfTI paths and PPMI tables under a data
# use agreement, so it must never be embedded as a gitlink in the site deploy.
spect-program/
# labOptimal does NOT belong in here — it lives at C:\Users\Auerbach\labOptimal
# with the other siblings. A second clone appeared here on 2026-09-05 and was
# removed the same day. This line is a guard so a repeat accident cannot be
# committed, not permission for the directory to exist.
labOptimal/
# Fallen-Heroes — the Ukrainian memorial gallery (github.com/ZachBach/Fallen-Heroes),
# cloned here 2026-09-06. Its own repo and its own remote; without this line
# `git add -A` from the root would embed it as a gitlink.
Fallen-Heroes/
# Aurelius Learn — the upstream for the /learn/ Lab app
# (github.com/ZachBach/aureliusLearn), added 2026-09-07. Same rule as the
# others: build there, copy the output into /learn/, and never let `git add -A`
# from the root swallow the repo as a gitlink. The DEPLOYED copy at /learn/ is
# tracked here; this source tree is not.
aureliusLearn/
# Vantage — Relic Field Terminal (github.com/ZachBach/-Vantage---Relic-Field-Terminal),
# cloned here 2026-09-08. Its own repo and its own remote, and it defaults to
# `main` while this repo is on `master`; without these lines `git add -A` from
# the root would embed it as a gitlink. Both spellings are ignored: a clone gets
# the dashed name, which shells read as an option, so the local folder is
# renamed to drop the leading dash.
-Vantage---Relic-Field-Terminal/
Vantage-Relic-Field-Terminal/

# Local working docs — checklists and notes, not part of the published site.
znatodos.md
handoff.md
zookahs-personal-guide-from-the-homie.md
# Draft article about the studio, for publishing elsewhere. Not site content.
aurelius-dynamic-article.md

# Git worktrees checked out from the nested echoGalaxy repo. Same reasoning
# as the line above — that repo's branches are its own business, and a
# worktree is just another view of them.
echoGalaxy.worktrees/

# Redesign prototype (parallax homepage) — local working copy, kept out of the
# published root site
prototype/

# Machine-local agent config (permission allowlist, local paths to other
# projects). The shared commands under .claude/commands/ stay tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json
# settings.json is nominally the *shared* settings file, but this machine's
# copy is an auto-accumulated permission allowlist full of absolute scratchpad
# paths and entries for files in other repos (MemorialLight.js lives in
# Fallen-Heroes). That is local noise, not project configuration, and it does
# not belong in a public repo. Delete the ignore line if a genuinely shared
# settings file is ever written by hand.
.claude/settings.json

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log
node_modules/

# Environment files — never in a public repo. No .env exists here today; this
# is the guard for the day one does, because `git add -A` does not ask.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# geo-lib bench artefacts. vendor/ is a copy of whatever three.js build the
# machine had; out/ is the rendered contact sheet. Both are regenerated by
# `node geo-lib/bench/render.mjs` and neither belongs in history — the vendored
# build in particular is a megabyte of somebody else's code that is already
# pinned in three places.
geo-lib/bench/vendor/
geo-lib/bench/out/
